      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "Alright.",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s03-t037"
    },
    {
      "_id": "37",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s03",
      "sequence_id": 38,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "Should I write this out on the shared doc, or just tell you the steps?",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s03-t038"
    },
    {
      "_id": "38",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s03",
      "sequence_id": 39,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "Sounds good — the shared doc works fine for this.",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s03-t039"
    },
    {
      "_id": "39",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s03",
      "sequence_id": 40,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "Okay, let me actually write this out step by step now.",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s03-t040"
    },
    {
      "_id": "40",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s03",
      "sequence_id": 41,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "Go ahead, start by subtracting 2x from both sides of 5x - 15 = 2x + 9.",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s03-t041"
    },
    {
      "_id": "41",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s03",
      "sequence_id": 42,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "That gives 3x - 15 = 9.",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s03-t042"
    },
    {
      "_id": "42",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s03",
      "sequence_id": 43,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "Now add 15 to both sides.",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s03-t043"
    },
    {
      "_id": "43",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s03",
      "sequence_id": 44,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "3x = 24, so dividing by 3 gives x = 8.",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s03-t044"
    },
    {
      "_id": "44",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s03",
      "sequence_id": 45,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "Great, that's the value of x locked in.",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s03-t045"
    },
    {
      "_id": "45",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s03",
      "sequence_id": 46,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "So now that we have x = 8, I want to understand why this method always works.",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s03-t046"
    },
    {
      "_id": "46",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s03",
      "sequence_id": 47,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "It works because both sides represent the same balance — whatever we do to one, we do to the other.",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s03-t047"
    },
    {
      "_id": "47",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s03",
      "sequence_id": 48,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "So subtracting 2x didn't change the equality, it just simplified which terms we're comparing.",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s03-t048"
    },
    {
      "_id": "48",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s03",
      "sequence_id": 49,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "Exactly — that's the core idea behind isolating a variable on either side.",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s03-t049"
    },
    {
      "_id": "49",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s03",
      "sequence_id": 50,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "What if we'd moved the 2x over before expanding, would that still work?",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s03-t050"
    },
    {
      "_id": "50",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s03",
      "sequence_id": 51,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "That's worth trying — let's see what happens if we do it that way.",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s03-t051"
    },
    {
      "_id": "51",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s03",
      "sequence_id": 52,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "So we'd have 5(x - 3) - 2x = 9, though it feels messier before expanding.",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s03-t052"
    },
    {
      "_id": "52",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s03",
      "sequence_id": 53,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "Maybe, but let's expand anyway and see where it leads.",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s03-t053"
    },
    {
      "_id": "53",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s03",
      "sequence_id": 54,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "5x - 15 - 2x = 9, which simplifies to 3x - 15 = 9.",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s03-t054"
    },
    {
      "_id": "54",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s03",
      "sequence_id": 55,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "That's the same equation as before, just reached differently.",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s03-t055"
    },
    {
      "_id": "55",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s03",
      "sequence_id": 56,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "So the order doesn't matter, we land on 3x - 15 = 9 either way.",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s03-t056"
    },
    {
      "_id": "56",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s03",
      "sequence_id": 57,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "Good work today, that's a solid way to close this one.",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s03-t057"
    },
    {
      "_id": "57",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s03",
      "sequence_id": 58,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "Yeah, this made a lot more sense once we saw both paths line up.",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s03-t058"
    },
    {
      "_id": "58",
